model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway.appCalls {
    metadata {
      constraint "Only a saved pool registration admits caching; similar authored app requirements run normally. The hosted pool overview caches the complete provider-enriched result only after fresh request authorization. Every warm load reads the four organization heads for accounts, observations, apps and membership plus Home history, skipping account resolution and provider calls. Fresh request authorization checks session validity before reuse; the cache key binds the current cookie, user, role and policy, so no separate user-session head is needed. A revoked original cookie is refused even after a warm fill. Changed or unavailable heads, policy or identity changes, app versions and presentation deadlines invalidate the result. Native report reuse ends at the SDK observation deadline, including the five-minute observedAt default. A write during a fill refuses the result. App pages and MCP share the configured official catalog reader. Model limits, scoped banked resets and provider badges stay visible; an absent icon uses the provider label. Query dispatch preserves account-required and version-changed failures; only cache storage failures become unavailable. Stale requests include dispatch timing and retain the version-change response. No storage migration or protocol change."
    }
  }
}
